# Canonical author identities.
#
# The entries below map identities that were recorded by mistake — commits made
# on machines where `git config user.name` / `user.email` had not been set, and
# commits tagged with the name of the tool that produced them — onto the single
# canonical identity of this repository's author.
#
# These are all the same person. No authorship is reassigned here: every commit
# listed on the right was written by Artem Arakcheev. Git history itself is
# unmodified; this file only affects how names are displayed by git log,
# git shortlog and git blame.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Recorded Name <recorded@email>

Artem Arakcheev <artarakcheev@gmail.com> Your Name <you@example.com>
Artem Arakcheev <artarakcheev@gmail.com> Your Name (aider) <you@example.com>
Artem Arakcheev <artarakcheev@gmail.com> Artem Arakcheev (aider) <artarakcheev@gmail.com>
Artem Arakcheev <artarakcheev@gmail.com> Artem Arakcheev <aaar@mail.ru>
